From: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: install CoreSight SSDT (CPUs + ETEs + sinks + funnel) for ACPI-booted CIX SKY1

CIX Orion O6 firmware boots Linux via ACPI but exposes neither
ACPI Processor() devices for the 12 cores nor any CoreSight nodes.
Without ACPI processor objects, per_cpu(processors) stays NULL and
the in-tree etm4x ACPI binding cannot resolve a logical CPU for ETE
devices; without sink/link nodes the ACPI-bound TMC/funnel drivers
(added in patches 0009/0010) have nothing to claim.

Embed and dynamically install an SSDT that declares:
  - 12 \\_SB.CPUx ACPI0007 processor devices (UID 0..11) each with
    an ARMHC500 ETE child;
  - one ARMHC9FF dynamic SoC funnel (CSF0 @ 0x180B0000);
  - three ARMHC97C TMC ETFs (ETF0 @ 0x18060000, ETF1 @ 0x180A0000,
    ETF2 @ 0x19000000);
  - one ARMHC501 TMC ETR (ETR0 @ 0x180C0000).

The standard ACPI processor driver populates per_cpu(processors),
the etm4x platform driver binds the ETEs, and the TMC/funnel ACPI
platform drivers (patches 0009/0010) bind the sinks and link.

STM (ARMHC502) and TRBE are intentionally absent; their drivers
need separate ACPI backports.

Signed-off-by: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
---
 src/drivers/acpi/Makefile         |   2 +
 src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c | 164 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 166  insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c

--- a/src/drivers/acpi/Makefile
+++ b/src/drivers/acpi/Makefile
@@ -133,2 +133,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_ACPI_VIOT)		+= viot.o
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_RISCV)		+= riscv/
+
+obj-$(CONFIG_ARCH_CIX)		+= sky1-coresight.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c
@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * sky1-coresight: install a CoreSight SSDT at boot on CIX SKY1.
+ *
+ * Orion O6 firmware exposes no ACPI nodes for CoreSight components and
+ * also no ACPI Processor() devices for the 12 CPU cores (CPUs come
+ * solely from MADT GICC entries). This driver installs an SSDT that
+ * declares ACPI0007 processor devices, ARMHC500 ETE children, the
+ * dynamic SoC funnel (ARMHC9FF), three TMC ETF sinks (ARMHC97C) and
+ * the TMC ETR sink (ARMHC501) so the in-tree drivers can bind.
+ *
+ * STM (ARMHC502) and TRBE are not declared here; their drivers in
+ * 6.6.x lack ACPI match tables and need separate backports.
+ */
+#include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <linux/init.h>
+#include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/printk.h>
